Meridian is distributed under two licences, split by component.

MODEL  ->  Apache License 2.0 (Apache-2.0)

    Covers everything except the user interface: the feed-reader model and its
    supporting code. In the source tree that is meridian/domain,
    meridian/application and meridian/infrastructure, together with
    meridian/main.py, meridian/version.py, the build scripts and the tests.
    This aligns with the MMSP specification ecosystem, which is Apache-2.0.
    Full text: LICENSE-APACHE-2.0.txt

USER INTERFACE  ->  GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0 (LGPL-3.0)

    Covers the PySide6 and Qt Quick layer (meridian/ui) only, licensed under the
    LGPL to align with Qt's own licensing. Full text: LICENSE-LGPL-3.0.txt,
    which incorporates the terms of the GPL-3.0 in LICENSE-GPL-3.0.txt.

The running application shows both under its header: "UI Licence" (LGPL-3.0)
and "Model Licence" (Apache-2.0).

